# Version bump on code changes

When you modify HKOCA toolkit code (Python modules, CLI, bundled R scripts, configs shipped in `hkoca/`, or Docker/conda wiring that affects releases), also update `hkoca/_version.py`.

- Increment the pre-release segment for functional changes in the same alpha line (e.g. `0.1.0-alpha.3` -> `0.1.0-alpha.4`).
- Include the version bump in the same commit as the code change (do not leave `_version.py` unstaged).
- Do not bump version for README-only or comment-only edits unless the user asks.

```python
# hkoca/_version.py
__version__ = "0.1.0-alpha.N"
```
